1
00:00:00,030 --> 00:00:01,680
An octopus has three hearts,

2
00:00:01,680 --> 00:00:02,770
and blue blood.

3
00:00:03,060 --> 00:00:05,050
Two of the hearts sit by the gills,

4
00:00:05,120 --> 00:00:07,450
pumping blood through them to pick up oxygen.

5
00:00:08,040 --> 00:00:10,690
The third, the biggest, sends it around the body.

6
00:00:10,930 --> 00:00:14,230
And that blood is blue because it carries oxygen on copper,

7
00:00:14,230 --> 00:00:16,070
not iron like ours.

8
00:00:16,500 --> 00:00:20,360
But here's the catch: every time an octopus jets through the water,

9
00:00:20,360 --> 00:00:22,010
that main heart pauses.

10
00:00:22,430 --> 00:00:24,690
That's why they'd rather crawl than swim.

11
00:00:24,910 --> 00:00:26,420
Swimming wears them out fast.

12
00:00:26,420 --> 00:00:29,210
So next time you see one zooming away,

13
00:00:29,250 --> 00:00:30,533
cut it some slack, because
